 "posts": [
  {
   "title": "Record Store Day: queue from 8am on Call Lane",
   "category": "events",
   "image": "shop-floor.jpg",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p class=\"\">Doors open at 8am on Saturday 18 April. One copy of each title per person, and nothing from the day goes online until Monday at 10am.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p class=\"\">Bring a flask. We will have tea from 7.30 for the front of the queue.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
  },
  {
   "title": "Listening night: Impulse! gatefolds, side two only",
   "category": "events",
   "image": "spinning.jpg",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p class=\"\">Thursday 2 October, 7pm to 9pm at Call Lane. Ines plays the second sides of eight Impulse! records on the shop console. Free, 30 places, first come.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
  },
  {
   "title": "Buying trip to Otley: 1,400 soul and funk 45s",
   "category": "shop-news",
   "image": "singles-case.jpg",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p class=\"\">We bought a collection of singles from a former DJ in Otley. They go out in boxes of 50 and on the singles wall from next Tuesday.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
  },
  {
   "title": "Folk crate moves to Hebden Bridge",
   "category": "shop-news",
   "image": "digging.jpg",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p class=\"\">From October the folk section lives at Market Street. Call Lane keeps a small crate of new folk pressings by the counter.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
  },
  {
   "title": "Cassette table, every Sunday in October",
   "category": "events",
   "image": "cassette.jpg",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p class=\"\">A table of used tapes at £2 each by the door on Sundays. Inlays included, no cases for the ones that arrived without.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
  },
  {
   "title": "Why we play every used record before it is priced",
   "category": "shop-news",
   "image": "hero.jpg",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p class=\"\">Grading by eye misses pressing faults, warps you can only hear, and the long scratch that looks like a hairline. So every used record goes on the shop deck for at least a minute a side.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p class=\"\">It is slower. It is also why our returns pile is small.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
  }
 ],
